<header><p class="st-kicker">khanate · Central Asia and the Steppe</p><h1 class="st-title">Khanate of Kokand</h1><p class="st-meta">1709 CE – 1876 CE · capital Kokand</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">An Uzbek khanate of the Ferghana valley that grew to rule Tashkent and the Kyrgyz and Kazakh steppes before Russia annexed it in 1876.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Around 1709 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shahrukh-bi">Shahrukh Bi</a>, leader of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ming-empire">Ming</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uzbeks">Uzbek</a> tribe, broke away from the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/khanate-of-bukhara">Khanate of Bukhara</a> and established a separate state in the eastern <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/principality-of-ferghana">Ferghana</a> valley. His successors built <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kokand">Kokand</a> as their capital, and Narbuta Bi strengthened the state in the late 18th century.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alim-khan-of-kokand">Alim Khan</a>, who took the title khan around 1800, created a standing army and conquered <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tashkent">Tashkent</a> in 1809. His brother and successor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/umar-khan-of-kokand">Umar Khan</a> was a patron of poetry whose wife <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nodira">Nodira</a> was a celebrated poet. The khanate controlled the trade routes to <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-shule">Kashgar</a> and dominated <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kyrgyz-people">Kyrgyz</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kazakhs">Kazakh</a> nomads, building forts such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kyzylorda">Ak-Mechet</a> on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/syr-darya">Syr Darya</a>. Rivalry between settled <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sarts">Sarts</a> and nomadic <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kipchaks">Kipchaks</a> caused civil wars.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a> took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kyzylorda">Ak-Mechet</a> in 1853 and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tashkent">Tashkent</a> in 1865. After a revolt against the pro-Russian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khudayar-khan">Khudayar Khan</a> in 1875, General <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mikhail-skobelev">Skobelev</a> crushed resistance and Russia annexed the khanate in 1876 as the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/principality-of-ferghana">Ferghana</a> Oblast of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/turkestan-governorate-general">Turkestan Governorate-General</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/khanate-of-kokand.jpg" alt="Khanate of Kokand" width="320" height="192"><figcaption>Image: Incall · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Banner_of_the_Kokand_Khans.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1709 CE – 1876 CE</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>khanate</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Kokand</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Shahrukh Bi, Alim Khan, Khudayar Khan</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Sunni Islam</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Uzbek, Persian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/uzbekistan">Uzbekistan</a>, <a href="/countries/kyrgyzstan">Kyrgyzstan</a>, <a href="/countries/tajikistan">Tajikistan</a>, <a href="/countries/kazakhstan">Kazakhstan</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Kokand Khanate, Khoqand</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1792&amp;focus=khanate-of-kokand" aria-label="Khanate of Kokand on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="6421 730 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Khanate of Kokand lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M6741 986L6588 1010M6741 986L7567 1068M6741 986L6487 457M6741 986L6691 960"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M6588 1010h0M7567 1068h0M6487 457h0M6691 960h0"/><path class="map-dot